<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tufa Poqiang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tufa Poqiang was a prince of the Southern Liang, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> kingdom in Qinghai, and the son of its last ruler Tufa Rutan. After Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> destroyed Southern Liang in 414 he fled to the Northern Wei, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> rulers shared his clan's origins; they gave him the name Yuan He, and he became a distinguished general and official in their service.</p></div>
